Package: os-latency-tests
Architecture: linux-any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: measure OS and hardware latencies from user space
 os-latency-tests runs micro-benchmarks for thread creation, blocking
 synchronisation wake-up and memory allocation, and reports full latency
 distributions (p50 to p99.99 and max) together with a description of the
 platform: CPU, cache hierarchy, kernel preemption model and available
 performance counters.
 .
 It is meant for comparing kernels (generic, low-latency, PREEMPT_RT) and
 boards, and for deriving low-latency design decisions from measured data.
 Results are written as JSON plus raw per-sample CSV for further analysis.
